      {
        "title": {
          "en": "Microsoft Research Introduces ADeLe for AI Performance Prediction",
          "zh": "微软研究院推出ADeLe，预测与解释AI性能"
        },
        "tl_dr": {
          "en": "Microsoft researchers, in collaboration with Princeton University and Universitat Politècnica de València, introduced ADeLe to predict and explain AI performance across tasks, addressing limitations of current benchmarks.",
          "zh": "微软研究院研究人员与普林斯顿大学及瓦伦西亚理工大学合作，推出了ADeLe，旨在预测和解释AI在不同任务中的表现，以解决当前基准测试的局限性。"
        },
        "key_takeaways": {
          "en": [
            "Current AI benchmarks report performance on specific tasks but provide limited insight into underlying capabilities, failing to explain failures or reliably predict new outcomes.",
            "ADeLe is designed to predict and explain AI performance across various tasks by offering deeper insights into an AI's underlying capabilities.",
            "The development of ADeLe is a collaborative effort between Microsoft researchers, Princeton University, and Universitat Politècnica de València."
          ],
          "zh": [
            "当前AI基准测试仅报告特定任务性能，但对潜在能力洞察有限，无法解释故障或可靠预测新结果。",
            "ADeLe旨在通过深入洞察AI的底层能力，预测和解释AI在不同任务中的表现。",
            "ADeLe的开发是微软研究院研究人员与普林斯顿大学及瓦伦西亚理工大学之间的合作成果。"
          ]
        },
        "impact": {
          "en": "This development aims to improve the understanding of AI model capabilities and limitations beyond simple benchmarks. Better insight into AI performance could facilitate more effective deployment and development of large language models in the industry.",
          "zh": "这一发展旨在超越简单的基准测试，增进对AI模型能力和局限性的理解。对AI性能的更深入洞察有助于行业内更有效地部署和开发大型语言模型。"
        },
        "source": "Microsoft Research",
        "link": "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/blog/adele-predicting-and-explaining-ai-performance-across-tasks/"
      },
      {
        "title": {
          "en": "OpenAI Models, Codex, and Agents Now Accessible on AWS",
          "zh": "OpenAI 模型、Codex 及代理现已可在 AWS 上使用"
